  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_020 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) at 0.706 accuracy. The key uncertainty is whether transformer aggregation, which underperformed avgpool for pca_n2000 (0.586 vs 0.635), might interact differently with the richer learned scvi_n200 representations. config_028 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) isolates this single change while keeping all other parameters at their best-known values. If transformer helps, it could push accuracy above 0.706; if not, it confirms avgpool is optimal for scvi_n200 and the remaining budget can target other refinements. Expected cost is moderate (~5-6 GPU hours, comparable to config_047 at 4.55 and config_020 at 4.82), leaving sufficient budget for one more experiment."
}

